        "original_id": "2cf468ee-b614-5cdd-afa4-50e8826164d8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hudson Austin, Maurice Bishop, Bernard Coard, Eric Gairy\n- Organizations: New Jewel Movement\n- Places: Grenada\n- Events: 13 March 1979 revolution, coup after Maurice Bishop’s killing\n- Roles: chairman, general, politician, leader\n\nFacts:\n- On 13 March 1979, the New Jewel Movement came to power in Grenada through a revolution that removed Eric Gairy from office.\n- Maurice Bishop was a Grenadian politician and the leader of the New Jewel Movement.\n- Maurice Bishop was associated with popular efforts in socio-economic development, education, and Black liberation.\n- After launching a coup within the revolutionary government, Bernard Coard held power for three days.\n- Bernard Coard was deposed by General Hudson Austin.\n- After the killing of Maurice Bishop, Hudson Austin formed a military government in Grenada and ruled it as chairman.",
